    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Three Daylamite brothers took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#fars">Fars</a>, the Jibal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#iraq">Iraq</a> between 934 and 945 and ruled them as a family confederation.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#shia-islam">Shia</a> themselves, they kept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sunni-islam">Sunni</a> Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#caliphate">caliphs</a> as figureheads in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#baghdad">Baghdad</a> for 110 years.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#adud-al-dawla">Adud al-Dawla</a> (d. 983) they reached their height; family rivalry then left them prey to the Ghaznavids and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The astronomer Abd al-Rahman al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sufism">Sufi</a> dedicated his Book of Fixed Stars to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#adud-al-dawla">Adud al-Dawla</a>; it contains one of the earliest recorded descriptions of the Andromeda Galaxy.</p></aside>
    </section>

